R22 FLIGHT SCHOOL
LINUX INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS

Default Port: 8086


==================================================
LINUX INSTALLATION
==================================================

R22 Flight School is designed for Debian-based Linux systems.


1. Download the latest R22 Flight School release ZIP.

Example:

R22_Flight_School_Production_v111.zip


2. Extract the ZIP.

Example:

unzip R22_Flight_School_Production_v111.zip


3. Enter the extracted folder.

Example:

cd R22_Flight_School_Production_v111


4. Make the Linux installer executable.

Run:

chmod +x INSTALL_LINUX.sh


5. Run the installer.

Run:

./INSTALL_LINUX.sh


If administrator privileges are required:

sudo ./INSTALL_LINUX.sh


6. Allow the installer to complete.

The installer will:

- Verify the application files
- Create the Python environment
- Install required dependencies
- Run the built-in application verification tests
- Prepare persistent application data
- Prepare offline training assets
- Configure local network access
- Preserve existing user and training data during upgrades

If application verification fails, the installer will stop.

Do not ignore a verification failure.


==================================================
STARTING R22 FLIGHT SCHOOL
==================================================

After installation, start R22 Flight School using the installed launcher or service.

Local computer:

http://127.0.0.1:8086


Other devices on the same network:

http://LINUX-IP-ADDRESS:8086


Example:

http://192.168.1.60:8086


==================================================
FINDING YOUR LINUX IP ADDRESS
==================================================

Run:

hostname -I


or:

ip addr


Find the LAN IP address for the computer running R22 Flight School.


Example:

192.168.1.60


From another computer, tablet, or phone on the same network, open:

http://192.168.1.60:8086


==================================================
LINUX FIREWALL
==================================================

If another device cannot connect, verify that TCP port 8086 is allowed through the Linux firewall.

R22 Flight School uses:

TCP 8086


If UFW is enabled, an administrator may allow the port with:

sudo ufw allow 8086/tcp


Do not expose R22 Flight School directly to the public Internet unless the network is properly secured.


==================================================
FIRST LOGIN
==================================================

Sign in using the initial administrator account created by the application.

If the default administrator password is still enabled, change it immediately.

Open:

Settings & Profile

Then change the administrator password.


==================================================
OFFLINE USE
==================================================

After installation, the core R22 Flight School training environment is designed to work without an Internet connection.

Offline features include:

- R22 POH Mastery
- Bundled R22 POH reference
- Ground-school lessons
- Question banks
- Practice exams
- Interactive Startup
- Cockpit Flow Trainer
- Rotor System Component Lab
- Flight Controls & Rotor Motion
- Emergency Procedures Trainer
- Weight & Balance
- Performance calculations
- Flashcards
- Oral and checkride preparation
- Student progress
- ATC training material
- Installed FAA chart material
- Local images and audio
- Application assets

Some optional connected resources may require Internet access.


==================================================
UPGRADING
==================================================

To install a newer release:

1. Download the new release ZIP.
2. Extract it into a new folder.
3. Make INSTALL_LINUX.sh executable if required.
4. Run the Linux installer.
5. Allow the installer to preserve existing application data.

Do not manually delete the application data directory unless you intentionally want to remove:

- User accounts
- Student progress
- Exam history
- POH Mastery progress
- Training records
- Settings
- Backups


==================================================
BACKUP
==================================================

Before major upgrades, create a backup from:

Admin > Backups


Backups can preserve:

- User accounts
- Student progress
- Scores
- Assignments
- Training history
- Application configuration


==================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
==================================================

INSTALLER VERIFICATION FAILED

If the installer reports:

Application verification failed

Do not ignore the error.

The installer intentionally stops when verification tests fail.

Copy the complete installer error output when reporting the problem.


PORT 8086 IS ALREADY IN USE

Run:

ss -ltnp | grep 8086


You can also use:

sudo lsof -i :8086


Stop the conflicting process before restarting R22 Flight School.


OTHER DEVICES CANNOT CONNECT

Verify:

- R22 Flight School is running
- Both devices are on the same network
- You are using the Linux server's LAN IP address
- TCP port 8086 is allowed through the firewall
- You are not using 127.0.0.1 from another device

127.0.0.1 always refers to the device you are currently using.


OLDER VERSION APPEARS AFTER AN UPGRADE

1. Close the browser tab.
2. Restart R22 Flight School.
3. Reopen the application.
4. Perform a hard refresh.

Chrome / Chromium:

Ctrl + Shift + R

Verify the installed version on the login screen.


